#. TRANSLATORS a switch under the heading "Checksum count": count the indexed checksums in a background job
msgid "Count in the background"
msgstr "Count in the background"

msgid "Counting the indexed checksums reads every one of them, which takes seconds on a large server. Switched on, a background job counts them once per interval, so the status never waits for it. Switched off, the status counts them when it is opened and the last count is older than the interval."
msgstr "Counting the indexed checksums reads every one of them, which takes seconds on a large server. Switched on, a background job counts them once per interval, so the status never waits for it. Switched off, the status counts them when it is opened and the last count is older than the interval."

