msgid "Every rule that can affect your files, in the order they are evaluated — the first match decides. Rules an administrator enforced come first and are read-only; your own rules come next and are yours to edit and reorder; the defaults below them apply only where none of your rules matched. You can create rules only if you have been given permission and the path is a folder in your own files that you can write to."
msgstr "Every rule that can affect your files, in the order they are evaluated — the first match decides. Rules an administrator enforced come first and are read-only; your own rules come next and are yours to edit and reorder; the defaults below them apply only where none of your rules matched. You can create rules only if you have been given permission and the path is a folder in your own files that you can write to."

